# Synapse i18n

## Locales

| Code | Variant |
|------|---------|
| `en` | English (source / fallback) |
| `pt` | European Portuguese (PT-PT), **pré-AO90** spelling |
| `es` | Spanish (Spain) |
| `fr` | French (France) |

Do not invent additional locales.

## Catalogs (`lib/i18n/`)

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `messages.ts` | Top-level namespaces (`nav`, `home`, `profile`, `authPages`, `common`) + wires catalogs |
| `chromeCatalog.ts` | Vault chrome, toolbars, toasts already under `chrome.*` |
| `settingsCatalog.ts` | Admin settings UI |
| `legendCatalog.ts` | Markdown help legend |
| `statusCatalog.ts` | Status / error / toast fallbacks under `status.*` |

## Hard rule

Never hardcode user-visible English in `app/**` or `components/**`. Add a key to the right catalog and translate **all four** locales (`en` / `pt` / `es` / `fr`). Prefer an existing exact `chrome.*` / `settings.*` key over duplicating into `status.*`.

Use `useI18n().t('namespace.key', { var })` (client components). Interpolation uses `{name}` placeholders.

## Portuguese (PT-PT pré-AO90)

- Spelling: actual, actualizado, activo/activa, projecto, seleccionar/seleccionado, acção/acções, secção/secções, directo, objecto.
- Do **not** hypercorrect words that already use ç: Ligações, Alterações, organizações, notificações.
- Progressive: **A + infinitive** (A carregar…, A guardar…) — never BR gerunds (Carregando, Salvando).
- Lexicon: utilizador, ficheiro, guardar, ecrã, palavra-passe, cofre, descarregar — never BR usuário/arquivo/salvar/tela/senha.

## Spanish (Spain) / French (France)

- ES: bóveda, papelera, contraseña, pulse/haga clic — not LatAm vault/computadora/celular.
- FR: coffre, corbeille, mot de passe, vouvoiement — not Quebec courriel.

## Product literals (keep in English)

Myelin, Synapse, Markdown, ZIP, SSO, Wiki, Other (YAML category key), wikilink syntax (`[[…]]`, `![[…]]`).

## Assistant replies

Agents still reply to the user in **English**. i18n rules apply to product UI copy only.
